Phasmid: WebRTC IP handling and public address

What:     The WebRTC IP handling policy comes from the profile. With
          network.webrtc.public_ip set, the mapped address in every STUN
          Binding success response without MESSAGE-INTEGRITY is replaced by
          it (port kept, FINGERPRINT recomputed), so srflx candidates carry
          the profile's address; a mapped address of the other family drops
          the response. Host candidates, ICE checks and TURN stay stock.
Why:      The srflx candidate exposes the host's public IP, which must match
          the proxy exit IP while WebRTC keeps working.
Profile:  network.webrtc.ip_handling_policy, network.webrtc.public_ip
Hooks:    chrome/browser/renderer_preferences_util.cc UpdateFromSystemSettings;
          services/network/p2p/socket_udp.cc P2PSocketUdp::HandleReadResult
Contexts: main, iframe; workers have no RTCPeerConnection
Guard:    tests/guards/network/webrtc.py

